 "result_text": "I fixed this in `aws_google_auth/__init__.py`. I haven't run it or the tests.\n\nThe cause was that when no profile was set, the tool printed the `export` lines and then still wrote to the AWS files. It used `None` as the profile name, which produced a `[None]` section in `~/.aws/credentials` and a `[profile None]` section in `~/.aws/config`.\n\nCredentials are now written to the files only when a profile is set (`-p` or `$AWS_PROFILE`). With no profile, the tool only prints the exports.\n\nAny `[None]` sections already in your `~/.aws/credentials` will stay there. You'll need to delete them by hand, along with `[profile None]` in `~/.aws/config`, before the aws-cli error goes away.",
